  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37215136",
      "title": "What's a Backend? And Why Would You Want One?",
      "lectureOrder": 223,
      "videoOrder": 207,
      "sourceHash": "ee7b0b3e9061df47b14cc738e483e433009a55a0370167217b0be9d6a2a6037f",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.21,
          "en": "So for this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.21,
          "end": 6.27,
          "en": "let's start with the most important question.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.27,
          "end": 11.27,
          "en": "What exactly is such a backend and why would we need one?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.7,
          "end": 13.47,
          "en": "Well, at this point in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.47,
          "end": 15.93,
          "en": "we, of course, built many Flutter apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.93,
          "end": 19.56,
          "en": "but there's one thing all these Flutter apps had in common.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.56,
          "end": 22.44,
          "en": "They, of course, run on the user's device,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.44,
          "end": 24,
          "en": "their mobile phone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 24,
          "end": 27.81,
          "en": "Therefore, any data that's generated by that app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.81,
          "end": 31.32,
          "en": "like for example, that list of grocery items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.32,
          "end": 35.79,
          "en": "any such data is stored locally on that device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.79,
          "end": 38.64,
          "en": "And therefore, if that device would be lost",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.64,
          "end": 42.93,
          "en": "or replaced or erased, all the data stored on it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.93,
          "end": 45.87,
          "en": "would be lost and erased as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.87,
          "end": 47.82,
          "en": "Now, for such a shopping list,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.82,
          "end": 50.64,
          "en": "that might not really be a problem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.64,
          "end": 52.8,
          "en": "but of course for other kinds of apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.8,
          "end": 55.32,
          "en": "that might be a huge problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.32,
          "end": 59.22,
          "en": "Another potential problem is that some apps actually need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 59.22,
          "end": 61.98,
          "en": "to share data with other users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.98,
          "end": 65.31,
          "en": "I mean, the Uber app wouldn't be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.31,
          "end": 68.88,
          "en": "that helpful if only you could use it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.88,
          "end": 73.14,
          "en": "Of course, your app must communicate with potential drivers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.14,
          "end": 76.59,
          "en": "and those drivers in the end communicate back to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.59,
          "end": 78.93,
          "en": "And the same is true for many other apps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.93,
          "end": 80.55,
          "en": "The Amazon app, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.55,
          "end": 83.58,
          "en": "would not work if it could only work with data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.58,
          "end": 86.19,
          "en": "that's stored locally on your device.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.19,
          "end": 89.28,
          "en": "Instead, the Amazon app needs to be able to reach out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.28,
          "end": 92.85,
          "en": "to Amazon's servers to load the data from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.85,
          "end": 94.65,
          "en": "And that's the entire idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.65,
          "end": 97.28999999999999,
          "en": "behind adding such a backend server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.28999999999999,
          "end": 100.38,
          "en": "The idea is that your app does not need to run",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 100.38,
          "end": 101.75999999999999,
          "en": "and work alone,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.75999999999999,
          "end": 105.96000000000001,
          "en": "but instead in conjunction with some services and data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.96000000000001,
          "end": 109.71000000000001,
          "en": "provided and stored on such backend servers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.71000000000001,
          "end": 114.39,
          "en": "So these servers are really just computers machines running",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.39,
          "end": 116.00999999999999,
          "en": "somewhere in the internet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.00999999999999,
          "end": 118.47,
          "en": "And of course, the exact configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.47,
          "end": 121.74,
          "en": "and which features a certain backend offers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.74,
          "end": 123.96,
          "en": "depends on the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.96,
          "end": 125.97,
          "en": "Maybe you built it yourselves,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 125.97,
          "end": 128.49,
          "en": "maybe you wrote your own backend logic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.49,
          "end": 131.28,
          "en": "maybe you're using some third party solution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.28,
          "end": 132.99,
          "en": "So that depends.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 132.99,
          "end": 135.18,
          "en": "But in the end, they will very likely",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.18,
          "end": 138.12,
          "en": "also store data in some database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 138.12,
          "end": 141.3,
          "en": "besides doing other work, which is also possible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.3,
          "end": 144.3,
          "en": "And since they do run in some data centers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144.3,
          "end": 146.46,
          "en": "somewhere in the internet, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 146.46,
          "end": 149.91,
          "en": "app users from the entire world can interact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 149.91,
          "end": 154.91,
          "en": "with the same data since it's stored in one central place,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 155.16,
          "end": 159.27,
          "en": "instead of on the mobile phones of your users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 159.27,
          "end": 162.27,
          "en": "Of course, your flutter app must be able to communicate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 162.27,
          "end": 166.17000000000002,
          "en": "with those backend servers to use their services and data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 166.17000000000002,
          "end": 170.67000000000002,
          "en": "And that communication typically happens via HTTP requests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 170.67000000000002,
          "end": 173.97,
          "en": "And that is exactly what we're going to take a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 173.97,
          "end": 176.43,
          "en": "at in this course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 176.43,
          "end": 179.28,
          "en": "We're not going to build a custom backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 179.28,
          "end": 182.61,
          "en": "because this course is not about backend development",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 182.61,
          "end": 185.46,
          "en": "or using other programming languages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 185.46,
          "end": 189.63,
          "en": "Instead, we'll use a very simple dummy third party service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.63,
          "end": 191.85,
          "en": "as a backend, but you will learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.85,
          "end": 195.06,
          "en": "how you can then send requests to that service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 195.06,
          "end": 199.07999999999998,
          "en": "to store data there or retrieve data from there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 199.07999999999998,
          "end": 201.6,
          "en": "And that, of course, will then also allow you to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.6,
          "end": 205.44,
          "en": "that knowledge that you do gain in this section to adapt it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.44,
          "end": 209.703,
          "en": "for other use cases where you might be using other backends.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
